Input

The input are in the following contents will be illustrated:

	Concept and Ideas. The idea of using a digital platform to improve disaster preparedness and response at the barangay level served as the foundation for the researchers' investigation. The researchers developed a web-based solution that emphasizes real-time communication and effective resource allocation after identifying the shortcomings of the current reporting systems,  including delays,  a lack of coordination,  and restricted accessibility. These ideas and concepts serve as the bedrock for developing new technologies and improving existing ones (Kharazishvili et al., 2021).

Related Literature and Studies. The primary purposes of reviewing literature is to identify gaps in existing knowledge and to propose future research directions (Ruiz et al., 2025). The researchers looked at a number of studies and publications pertaining to crisis informatics, information systems, and disaster management in order to fortify the system's framework. In order to reduce risks and increase efficiency, prior research has highlighted the significance of incorporating contemporary technology into local government disaster response. The platform is evidence-based and in line with best practices thanks to the insightful information gleaned from these studies, which helped shape system features like resource monitoring, incident reporting, and communication channels.

Web Development Tools. he researchers used contemporary web development tools that support security, scalability, and responsive design 23 when creating the B-READY system. While backend frameworks like Node.js or Django guaranteed dependable server-side operations, frontend technologies like HTML5, CSS, and JavaScript made it possible to create user- friendly interfaces. Disaster reports and user information were safely stored in a relational database. These tools ensured a dependable and maintainable solution by offering a stable environment for system implementation, debugging, and testing. By eradicating the silos between front end and back end development, these advanced tools empower developers to navigate complexities with unprecedented agility and precision. This exploration delves into the journey of these advanced tools, charting their evolution and elucidating their pivotal role in reshaping the fabric of web application development (Vasuki et. al., 2024).

Internet Connectivity and Network Infrastructure. For the system to be deployed, reliable internet access and a well-functioning network infrastructure were crucial. Residents, local officials, and responders were able to engage with the system without major delays thanks to the platform's support for real-time data transmission made possible by internet access. Accessibility, data integrity, and system resilience were further guaranteed by cloud hosting and secure server configurations, especially during emergency situations with high traffic volumes. Internet connectivity and robust network infrastructure are fundamental enablers of digital transformation across various sectors (Gabarró, 2020).

Process

	In the process illustrated by following the step:

Initial Planning. To make sure the system meets the unique requirements of barangay disaster management, the researchers started by establishing goals, specifying the project's scope, and identifying success indicators. Initial planning provides a structured framework for making informed decisions and allocating resources effectively (McClung et al., 2020).

Planning. To involve a systematic approach to defining the objectives, scope, and success metrics specifically tailored for Barangay disaster management. By integrating web engineering principles like rapid development, high user interaction, and scalability, the system's adaptability and security are ensured. This process creates a clear path for making informed decisions and allocating resources efficiently, supporting real-time feedback capabilities. Effective planning is essential for the system's ability to provide timely and reliable support during disaster events (Chahar & Singh, 2024).

Requirements. To pinpointing precise needs and functionalities to suit the available resources and skills for a web-based disaster response system. This process guarantees that the system is in sync with the specific demands of Barangay disaster management through iterative adjustments based on user feedback. The main goal is to direct the development process, ensuring the system achieves its objectives and offers reliable support for real-time disaster response. Clear requirements are crucial for the system's effectiveness in supporting disaster management efforts (Okesola et al., 2020).

Analysis & Design. To translates gathered requirements into a structured framework that guides the creation of the web-based disaster reporting and response system. This involves developing models and designs that address user, business, and governance needs, ensuring the system effectively supports Barangay disaster management. This phase provides a detailed blueprint for development, ensuring the system is comprehensive and aligned with its intended purpose (Shrestha, et al., 2020).

Implementation. Putting strategies into action to bridge the gap between research and practical use in a real-time Barangay disaster reporting system. This includes using stakeholder engagement, process mapping, and problem-solving to ensure the system is adopted effectively. This ensures the system is integrated into daily disaster response operations, enhancing its utility and impact (Lu, et al., 2021).

Testing. The formal process of verifying and validating the software to ensure it meets specifications and aligns with customer needs. In the context of a Barangay disaster reporting system, testing involves creating and running test cases to confirm the system's functionality, reliability, and performance. This process ensures that the system effectively supports disaster response and meets user needs (Mohapatra, 2025).

Evaluation. Identifying areas for improvement in the system through techniques like process mining. For a Barangay disaster reporting system, this means assessing performance, finding areas for enhancement, and gathering feedback from experts and users. This ensures that the system is continuously improved to meet the evolving needs of disaster management (Erdogan, et al., 2022).

Deployment. Making independently deployable services available for use in a real-time Barangay disaster reporting system. This includes launching the system's components to ensure they are accessible and operational for users. This ensures the system can assist in disaster management, providing real-time support and information to those who need it (Panogoulias, et al., 2022).

Output

In the output the following system will be illustrated: 

B-READY: A Web-Based System for Real-Time Barangay Disaster Reporting and Response. The study's final product is a useful web-based application that lets local officials and responders effectively manage, monitor, and respond to incidents while also enabling residents to submit disaster reports promptly and accurately. With features like real-time notifications, data analytics, and live mapping, the system offers a dependable platform that improves disaster preparedness and response at the barangay level.

The primary output is a fully developed and tested web system, ready for deployment. This includes the operational Victim and Rescue Team dashboards, a secure login/signup system, the real-time mapping module integrated with the Google Maps API, and the incident reporting module with media upload. The system's effectiveness, having been evaluated against ISO/IEC 25010 standards, provides a concrete, technology-based solution to the documented communication and coordination gaps in barangay-level disaster management.

Significance of the Study

The significance of this research aims to strengthen disaster preparedness, improve real-time reporting, and enhance community resilience at the barangay level. Here, the researchers outline the key terms and concepts that underpin this study:

Barangay Officials and Local Government Units (LGUs). The system is essential for enabling immediate disaster reporting, faster decision-making, and better coordination during emergencies. It equips them with accurate, timely data, allowing them to respond more efficiently and fulfil their mandate in protecting the community.

Community Residents. The website empowers residents to actively participate in disaster preparedness and response by instantly reporting incidents and receiving timely alerts, helping them make informed decisions and stay safe during emergencies.

Emergency Responders and Disaster Risk Reduction Management (DRRM). This system provides responders with rapid access to verified incident information, enabling faster interventions that can save lives and minimize property damage.

Students. Students gain practical knowledge about disaster preparedness and the role of technology in community safety, enhancing their awareness and readiness to contribute to emergency response efforts. 

Teachers. Educators can integrate the system into disaster preparedness lessons and drills, providing students with hands-on experience in using technology for real-world problem-solving in emergency situations. 

Future Researchers. This research contributes to the body of knowledge on localized disaster management systems and can serve as a foundation for future studies on enhancing real-time communication, reporting, and community engagement during disasters. 



Scope and Delimitation of the Study

This study aims to develop a web-based system for real-time barangay disaster reporting and response, designed to equip local officials and authorized administrators with a secure platform for receiving, verifying, and responding to incident reports both online and on-site. The system strengthens disaster preparedness, improves coordination, and enhances community safety by enabling residents to submit timely reports and barangay officials to immediately act upon them, whether through digital communication or direct physical rescue operations. It aligns with existing barangay disaster risk reduction protocols, ensuring that reports lead to rapid and organized action. 

The focus of the system is on collecting and processing disaster-related reports from residents, which are transmitted exclusively to authorized administrators for prompt decision-making and deployment of appropriate responses. This secure, admin-only access safeguards sensitive information and prevents misinformation, though it also means the public cannot view or track all submitted reports. The system does not cover national-level disaster reporting and is limited to the jurisdiction of participating barangays. Its effectiveness may depend on internet connectivity, the accuracy of user-submitted information, and the availability of trained responders and resources during emergencies. While external factors such as severe infrastructure damage or network outages may affect operations, the platform serves as a vital bridge between community reporting and immediate, coordinated disaster response efforts.



Definition of Terms

	The following section provides definitions for critical terminology to ensure clarity and consistency in discussing key concepts relate to web-based system disaster reporting and response. 

Barangay. Barangay is the smallest administrative division, similar to a village or district. It serves as the primary unit for implementing government policies, projects, and services at the local level. (Watanabe, 2025). For this research, conducted in sample Brgy. Apokon, the barangay serves as the fundamental unit for collecting and disseminating real-time disaster information. Its purpose within the web-based system is to facilitate immediate, localized reporting and response to ensure community safety and resilience.

Web-Based System. The Web System Development Process includes creating, updating, and managing websites or platforms, offering a reliable and secure environment that controls data flow and provides commercial advantages over desktop applications due to its accessibility and flexibility. This system enhances mobile working, system integration, and browser compatibility, allowing access from any device and supporting flexible work arrangements that boost employee productivity. Consequently, Web Systems offer uniformity for each user, simplifying issue resolution and enabling the conversion of most desktop software for use on any mobile device. (Jean, P., & Martin, F., 2023)

Real-Time Reporting. Real-Time Reporting involves delivering up-to-the-minute data as it's generated, enabling immediate insights and informed decision-making. This approach provides a continuous flow of information, ensuring stakeholders have the most current view of operations and performance. Real-time reporting refers to the immediate collection, analysis, and presentation of data as events unfold. Key concepts include data automation, live dashboards, and instant alerts, all of which enhance operational efficiency (Bradley, K., 2025)

Disaster Reporting. Disaster Reporting conceptually refers to the immediate and continuous flow of information regarding disasters from residents to the barangay administrator. This real-time reporting facilitates swift assessment, response coordination, and resource allocation to mitigate the impact of disasters within the community. Disaster reporting, as explored in the context of web-based systems, involves the fast and accurate generation of impact reports by extracting and curating information from the web to aid in humanitarian assistance planning (Grace, C., Paul, D., & et. al., 2023.



Chapter 2

MATERIALS AND METHODS

This chapter presents the research design, research subject, research instrument, process model, data collection procedure, data analysis, safety precautions, and ethical considerations that were followed by the researcher in this study.

Research Design

	This study employed developmental research to create a website-based platform for real-time disaster and accident reporting and response. According to Retno, et al. (2024), developmental research involves a structured design and evaluation methodology to develop innovative tools and models. By following this approach, the study aimed to provide practical solutions to common challenges faced by residents and emergency responders in a specific barangay. Through comprehensive analysis and rigorous testing, the research sought to ensure the website's effectiveness in real-world applications.

Additionally, Menezes and Salgado framework on Product Design and Development supports this study by providing a systematic approach to creating functional products (Menezes, & Salgado, 2024). This framework is particularly relevant as it emphasizes adapting strategies to meet user needs. The study's goal of building a user-centered platform for real-time reporting and response aligns with Dhore's methodology. By integrating this approach, the research ensures the website is both practical and market-ready. This comprehensive development strategy enables the website to effectively meet real-time reporting and response needs.

Research Subject

	The research investigation will be conducted among local government personnel in Barangay Apokon, with a primary focus on evaluating their current brgy. officials during disasters and accidents. To facilitate a holistic assessment of the product’s viability, the research team will engage a diverse group of stakeholders, including ICT Teachers with expertise in information technology, who will provide valuable insights on the product’s pedagogical and technical merits. Additionally, specialists from City Disaster Risk Reduction Management (CDRRM) will contribute their extensive knowledge on risk mitigation strategies and emergency preparedness measures (Sarmiento, 2024). The community members, being the primary end-users, will play a pivotal role in testing the product’s functionality and user experience within the context of a disaster reporting platform. By adopting this multi-pronged approach, the researchers will aim to develop a solution that is both efficacious and intuitive for its target audience.

