	For this study, a total of 48 individuals will participate, chosen through a blend of selective accessible sampling techniques. This methodology will ensure a broad spectrum of viewpoints from various stakeholders. The participants will be grouped into four categories based on their roles, professional roles and specialized knowledge.

Process Model

	The researchers adopted the Iterative Development Model for the design and creation of the B-READY system. This software development life cycle (SDLC) approach is characterized by cyclical prototyping, where a basic version of the software is built, tested, and then progressively refined with enhanced features and functionality in repeated cycles. This model was chosen to prioritize the development of a core, functional application for real-time reporting and response, allowing for continuous feedback and improvement throughout the project lifecycle, ensuring the final product is robust and closely aligned with user needs (Bahure, 2022). The iterative cycle is visualized in Figure 2.













