The research timeline was also included in the planning, where Table 2 presented the timeline of work phases, with a Gantt chart serving as a crucial planning and monitoring tool for the researchers. It helped estimate project duration, allocate resources, and determine task sequences while managing dependencies between tasks. Additionally, the chart allowed researchers to track progress, ensuring milestones were met on time. If delays occurred, it 32 enabled quick identification of issues, allowing researchers to take corrective action and keep the project on course.

Requirements

The functional requirements were derived from the study's objectives and specified features, encompassing user authentication, role-based dashboards, real-time GPS mapping, and an incident reporting module with media upload. Non-functional requirements focused on usability, reliability, real-time performance, and data security.



