In Progress

4

Real-time features, notification system

Planned



Iteration 1. This first iteration, "Foundation and Basic Structure," centers on establishing the core system. The process involves setting up the development environment with a React frontend and a Node.js backend. It also entails implementing the basic project structure and routing mechanisms, while creating the initial database schema in Firebase Firestore. Furthermore, this phase includes developing a basic prototype for the user authentication system.

	Iteration 2. The second iteration focuses on User Interface and Basic Functionality, concentrating on the development of the core user interfaces and features. This phase involves implementing the Victim Dashboard with its critical SOS functionality and developing the layout for the Rescue Team Dashboard. It also includes creating the incident reporting form with disaster-type buttons and building the basic user profile management system.

A.  Core Module Development

This phase focuses on the development of the application's three core foundational modules.

A.1 Authentication System Implementation

	The team develops a secure login and signup system using Firebase Authentication. This implementation includes user registration with email verification, secure password encryption, and session management. Furthermore, it establishes role-based access control to differentiate between victims and rescue teams and incorporates essential user convenience features such as a "remember me" option and a password recovery system.



A.2 Dashboard Development

The project implements two specialized dashboards, each with distinct functionalities tailored to their users. The Victim Dashboard features a header with a user greeting and notification indicators, a prominently placed SOS button for emergency reporting, a sidebar for navigation, and a main content area with a prototype for live map integration. Conversely, the Rescue Team Dashboard is equipped with a mission alert system, a resource management interface, a team communication panel, and a real-time map for tracking incidents.

A.3 Map Integration and Location Services

	The system integrates the Google Maps API to provide essential location services. This integration delivers base mapping functionality with defined barangay boundaries and uses the browser's GPS for location capture. It enables the placement of markers for incident locations and includes basic map controls and zoom functionality for user navigation.

